/A 1101 0 R
/Alt (Infographic summarizing caffeine toxicity, including its chemical structure, key mechanisms \(adenosine receptor antagonism, PDE inhibition, increased calcium release, acetylcholinesterase inhibition, and GABA-A antagonism\), and related toxicity levels. Below, diagrams illustrate five clinical manifestations: neurological \(anxiety, agitation, insomnia, seizures\), cardiovascular \(sinus tachycardia, arrhythmias, hypotension\), metabolic \(hypokalemia\), musculoskeletal \(tremor, muscle rigidity\), and respiratory \(hyperventilation\).)
